d you look to when you picked  up these books that you read and you  read the books and you made pencil marks  in them is it because you absorb the  lesson there or did it really not become  a permanent lesson and was just  something that you checked and it was  like a reflex so I have many specific  questions about many specific events and  people and circumstances that I have  tried to figure out with the surviving  source materials that we have in  abundance but I would still like to  delve into his mindset and reconstruct  his mind the closer you get to Stalin in  some ways the more elusive he can become  and especially around World War two  you've already illuminated a lot of  interesting aspects about Stalin's role  in the war but it would be interesting  to ask even more questions about how  seat-of-the-pants or deliberate some of  the decisions have been  you
 

